        "id": 1936647
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-04T18:26:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe after the conversation I had with hsz@ that in Android they do the equivalent of calling `set_connectable(true)` unconditionally when the stack comes up and keep that throughout runtime. Looking at their code it seems that there are a few instances where they choose specialized scan modes, but for the most part it seems to be left connectable indefinitely. Looking at that I think to match them we would just call `set_connectable(true)` either on instantiation or whenever enable is called.\n\nSetting connectable when started: https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/btservice/AdapterProperties.java;l\u003d1069?q\u003dSCAN_MODE_CONNECTABLE\u0026ss\u003dpiper%2FGoogle%2Faosp-master:packages%2Fmodules%2FBluetooth%2Fandroid%2Fapp%2Fsrc%2Fcom%2Fandroid%2Fbluetooth%2F",
      "parentUuid": "3813629d_27c7a3bf",
